# *_TO_STRING and STRING_TO_*. Implementation-defined: ed.3 table 22
# lists the conversions but the text format of the string (sign, leading
# zeros, spaces) is implementer-specific. The records are what IronPLC
# does; the plain decimal with a leading minus is also what matiec and
# RuSTy produce where they support the conversion.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: i
outputs: s_i back s_d
status: implementation-defined
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.2.5.1 table 22 (conversions to and from STRING)
---
0 i=42   => s_i='42' back=42 s_d='-2147483648'
1 i=-7   => s_i='-7' back=42 s_d='-2147483648'
2 i=0    => s_i='0' back=42 s_d='-2147483648'
